About CryptoKorr

CryptoKorr is the codename for a non-custodial control plane that lets
AI agents propose on-chain treasury actions while every decision is
evaluated against explicit policy, trust, screening, simulation, and
audit gates. The control plane (Phoenix) decides; a separate TypeScript
adapter executes through scoped, revocable smart-account permissions.
CryptoKorr never holds user funds or private keys.

This project depends on and integrates with third-party software,
protocols, and services. Each such dependency is governed by its own
license and terms. A non-exhaustive list of components and integration
points whose names are referenced in this repository for interoperability
purposes only includes:

  - Ethereum, ERC-4337, and ERC-7579 specifications and reference
    implementations.
  - Kernel smart-account contracts and the ZeroDev permission system.
  - Base and Base Sepolia (Coinbase / Optimism / OP Stack).
  - 0x, 1inch, Jupiter, and Circle CCTP routing and bridging APIs.
  - Morpho protocol contracts and the Morpho GraphQL API.
  - The Elixir/Phoenix framework and the Oban background-job system.
  - The Node.js / TypeScript runtime and its ecosystem packages.

